From: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>
Subject: ABI workaround for missing v4l2_async_register_subdev symbol
Patch-mainline: Never, kABI workaround
References: CVE-2026-68205 bsc#1274934

The patch
  patches.suse/media-v4l-async-Set-owner-for-async-sub-devices.patch
changed the exported symbol v4l2_async_register_subdev to
__v4l2_async_register_subdev.

Provide the old function (but with a warning message) for kABI
compatibility, just calling the new function with NULL module.

Signed-off-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>
Reviewed-by: Petr Pavlu <petr.pavlu@suse.com>

---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-async.c |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-async.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-async.c
@@ -932,6 +932,15 @@ static void __exit v4l2_async_exit(void)
 subsys_initcall(v4l2_async_init);
 module_exit(v4l2_async_exit);
 
+/* FIXME: for kABI workaround, provide the original version */
+#undef v4l2_async_register_subdev
+int v4l2_async_register_subdev(struct v4l2_subdev *sd)
+{
+	pr_warn("Unfixed v4l2_async_register_subdev is used\n");
+	return __v4l2_async_register_subdev(sd, NULL);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(v4l2_async_register_subdev);
+
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Guennadi Liakhovetski <g.liakhovetski@gmx.de>");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Sakari Ailus <sakari.ailus@linux.intel.com>");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Ezequiel Garcia <ezequiel@collabora.com>");
